WEBVTT

00:15:29.333 --> 00:15:32.059
JB: I think I've just found
the more creative you can get,

00:15:32.083 --> 00:15:34.143
the more options
you can present out there,

00:15:34.167 --> 00:15:36.434
it actually gets the dialog
going that much more

00:15:36.458 --> 00:15:38.601
and you truly understand what's important

00:15:38.625 --> 00:15:40.726
for the player and the agent.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.226
AG: One of Jason's
first opportunities to try it out

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:47.018
was in Pittsburgh with a player
who was recovering from shoulder surgery.

00:15:47.042 --> 00:15:49.684
JB: The agent knew
that he didn't have a lot of leverage

00:15:49.708 --> 00:15:51.893
and I remember
pushing really hard on salary

00:15:51.917 --> 00:15:56.476
and it was below what players
where he was drafted were receiving,

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:58.268
and we came to an agreement,

00:15:58.292 --> 00:16:01.268
but he was certainly
very disappointed at the agent.